H. 
Ministerial and Conforming Revisions 
Trans Bay has also made several ministerial or conforming revisions to either clarify or 
correct its tariff language or to better clarify the Trans Bay Tariff’s relation to the CAISO Tariff.  
These include: 
 Updating the Table of Contents; 
 Clarifying in Section 1 that Trans Bay does not provide retail electric service; 
 Clarifying in Section 1.3 how End-Users access the CAISO Controlled Grid; 
 Updating the definition of Ancillary Services in Section 3.3; 
 Updating the definition of Available Transfer Capacity in Section 3.5; 
 Updating the definition of Congestion Management in Section 3.12;  
 Updating the definition of Dispatch in Section 3.18; 
 Updating the definition of End-Use Customer or End-User in Section 3.21; 
 Updating the definition of Facilities Study Agreement in section 3.27; 
 Updating the definition of Generating Unit in Section 3.32; 
 Updating the definition of Good Utility Practice in Section 3.34; 
 Updating the definition of Interest in Section 3.46 to align with CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Local Publicly Owned Electric Utility in Section 3.53; 
 Updating the definition of Metered Subsystem in Section 3.60; 
 Updating the definition of Non-Load-Serving Participating TO in Section 3.65 to 
align with CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Non-Spinning Reserve in Section 3.67 to align with 
CAISO Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Spinning Reserve in Section 3.86 to align with CAISO 
Tariff; 
 Updating the definition of Utility Distribution Company in Section 3.99; 
 Defining FILI Service in Section 3.30 consistent with the CAISO Tariff; 
 Clarifying Gross Load’s definition in Section 3.35 to better match CAISO; 
 Revising the definition of “Interconnection” in Section 3.42 to address a 
typographical error; 
 Defining Interconnection Facilities in Section 3.45 to provide clarity; 
 Defining Point of Interconnection in Section 3.73 to align with CAISO; 
 Updating the definition of Regulation in Section 3.78; 
 Revising the definition of Reliability Upgrade in Section 3.81 to refer to a 
“facility” rather than an undefined term;
